WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.136
-My next guest is one of
the most successful writers

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:05.004
and producers working today.

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:07.640
He's the Emmy-nominated creator
of "Black-ish,"

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.976
and he also produces
the new show, "We The People,"

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:12.378
which premieres July 4th
on Netflix.

00:00:12.378 --> 00:00:15.148
Everyone please welcome
Kenya Barris.

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:16.515
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.515 --> 00:00:20.953
-♪ It's Kenya Barris,
case you didn't know ♪

00:00:20.953 --> 00:00:24.958
♪ Leo is his sign,
"Black-ish" is his show ♪

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:26.592
♪ It's Kenya Barris ♪

00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:28.961
♪ He's macking like a truck ♪

00:00:28.961 --> 00:00:30.863
♪ On the show about his life ♪

00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:34.734
♪ And it's called
"Black as...Can Be" ♪

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:37.202
-[ Laughing ]
-That's Kenya Barris.

00:00:37.202 --> 00:00:40.640
-Oh.
-It's so great to see you.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.275
Thank you so much --
-This is crazy.

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:44.110
-Thank you so much
for coming on the show.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.612
I appreciate this, bud.
-Thank you for having me, man.

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:47.780
-Oh, please.
We're giant fans.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.448
But obviously, they are,
as well.

00:00:49.448 --> 00:00:51.084
Standing up. Not bad.
-That's amazing.

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:53.219
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:56.022
-I like this.
What made you go blonde?

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:57.390
Is this a new thing?

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:00.326
-I think it was like
a mid-pandemic life crisis.

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:02.195
[ Laughter ]
I was like...

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.796
-It looks good!
-I had nothing going on,

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:05.498
I was like, "You know..."
It's been okay.

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:08.601
I got some likes,
a lot more hates, but...

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:11.471
-Yeah, you take the good
with the bad.

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:13.873
Last time we talked, we were
talking about your show.

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:17.109
And, yeah,
say hi to The Roots. Sure.

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:20.713
Actually, we were talking
about The Roots.

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:23.716
You did a whole special
on Juneteenth.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.651
-Juneteenth!
-Juneteenth.

00:01:25.651 --> 00:01:27.087
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:30.190
-You did a whole thing
about Juneteenth.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:33.392
And then, today, actually --
As of today --

00:01:33.392 --> 00:01:36.295
actually, today, it became
a national holiday.

00:01:36.295 --> 00:01:38.865
-Yes, it is a national --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:42.201
-I would say that you had a
little bit to, uh --

00:01:42.201 --> 00:01:44.804
maybe, to do with it.
-I don't know if we had

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:46.839
anything to do with helping it.
I don't think we hurt it,

00:01:46.839 --> 00:01:49.609
but I definitely feel like
if we were the butterfly wings

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:52.312
that helped start the tornado,
or whatever the case may be.

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:58.317
But, honestly, you guys,
they did a song that was amazing

00:01:58.317 --> 00:02:00.252
and came through in
an important time.

00:02:00.252 --> 00:02:02.722
It's just the whole episode
that we did.

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:04.924
And just to be a part of --

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:06.893
There's been a lot of things
that I've been --

00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:09.162
never thought I would be able
to be a part of.

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:13.032
And Pharrell's been with me.
But to be a part of something

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:17.337
that celebrates
our contribution --

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:18.837
you know what I'm saying? --
"our" meaning Black culture's

00:02:18.837 --> 00:02:22.508
contribution to all of
America -- you know? --

00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:25.178
I feel like there's nothing
that, like, to me --

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:27.814
It's in the very, very top of
the list of things I'm proud of.

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:29.782
-Thank you
for doing what you do.

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:31.184
Yeah.
-A lot of work to do.

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:33.353
-Yeah.
Speaking of work,

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:34.954
during the pandemic, you go,

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:36.455
"Yeah, we're still
gonna do shows.

00:02:36.455 --> 00:02:38.491
We're gonna give you
what you like.

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.326
We're going make more episodes
of 'Black-ish.'"

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:42.061
-Right.
-During a pandemic,

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:44.297
which is impossible,
but you said,

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:45.431
"No, nothing's impossible."

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.399
The first two episodes
you made animated.

00:02:47.399 --> 00:02:49.769
-Right. We wanted to --
We were --

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:52.872
Karey Burke and all those guys
over at ABC,

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:56.075
we were like -- We're lucky
enough to kind of be one of

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:58.277
the only shows on network
television that actually

00:02:58.277 --> 00:03:00.079
talks about things,
and we felt like it was

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:02.848
really important to still be
in that conversation

00:03:02.848 --> 00:03:04.350
with everything
that was going on,

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:07.453
with the civil unrest and just
with our political process.

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:11.390
And we felt like we didn't want
to have any hiccups with COVID

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:13.159
and things like that.
So we knew animation was one of

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:15.328
the things that kept going on,

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:17.429
and they let us do
an animated episode.

00:03:17.429 --> 00:03:19.699
-It's brilliant.
-It came out really good.

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:22.401
That show is just the gift
that keeps giving.

00:03:22.401 --> 00:03:24.270
-Yeah, we've known Anthony
for a long time.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:27.140
I love him.
Anything Anthony does,

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.008
I just love him, yeah.
This is --

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:30.910
You're going into the eighth
and final season.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:32.612
-Yeah.
-So this is it, going --

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:35.447
But it's bittersweet, right?
-It is bittersweet.

00:03:35.447 --> 00:03:37.784
We're really lucky
because shows --

00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:39.986
One, to be a Black show
that came on after

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:42.888
"Modern Family" was amazing.
It was really important to us

00:03:42.888 --> 00:03:45.758
to say that we wanted to speak
to the world --

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:47.326
you know what I'm saying? --
and talking about our culture.

00:03:47.326 --> 00:03:49.395
We didn't want to hide it.
We wanted it to be a show

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:53.666
that was absolutely, positively
about a 100% Black family.

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:55.668
You don't get to say goodbye.
Sometimes you're just canceled.

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:57.970
But to be able
to walk the show home

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:00.172
and give the audience
who's supported us this long

00:04:00.172 --> 00:04:03.242
a proper goodbye means a lot.
And hopefully, we can get you

00:04:03.242 --> 00:04:04.810
and The Roots and everybody to
come be a part

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:06.579
of this last season
in a big way.

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:08.348
-Yeah.
You kind of said Roots

00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:09.515
more than you said me,
but it's okay.

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:11.283
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.283 --> 00:04:13.719
I take that as an invite.

00:04:13.719 --> 00:04:16.922
I want to talk about
"We The People," on Netflix.

00:04:16.922 --> 00:04:18.757
I love that you're doing this.

00:04:18.757 --> 00:04:20.559
I think it's the best.

00:04:20.559 --> 00:04:23.495
You know, I think of
"Schoolhouse Rock."

00:04:23.495 --> 00:04:26.098
-Yes.
-When I had that growing up,

00:04:26.098 --> 00:04:29.668
and I loved it, and that's how
I learned, really.

00:04:29.668 --> 00:04:32.538
I mean, obviously my teachers,
as well, but -- yeah.

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:34.273
[ Laughter ]
Please, oh my gosh.

00:04:34.273 --> 00:04:36.375
To all my teachers out there,
I learned from you, obviously,

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:39.512
and my parents.
But "I'm Just a Bill"?

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:42.114
-I mean, that was it.
-That's how I know that.

00:04:42.114 --> 00:04:43.649
-It told me how,
when the thing was going,

00:04:43.649 --> 00:04:45.818
I'm like, "Hold on.
Because he's just a bill."

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:47.820
I would remember it, like --
You know what I'm saying? Yeah.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.154
-Is that kind of where
it came from?

00:04:49.154 --> 00:04:51.423
-So I was at this thing,
the Annenberg Foundation

00:04:51.423 --> 00:04:53.258
hosts this thing,
and Norman Lear had invited me.

00:04:53.258 --> 00:04:56.262
It was amazing.
And, you know,

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:58.764
one of my friends, Chris Nee,
who created this amazing show,

00:04:58.764 --> 00:05:00.199
"Doc McStuffins,"
which I think is the

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:02.201
longest-running animated show
on Disney.

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:06.138
-Of course, "Doc McStuffins."
-And we found out,

00:05:06.138 --> 00:05:07.907
because they bring in all these
people to give you, you know,

00:05:07.907 --> 00:05:09.008
lectures and things like that.

00:05:09.008 --> 00:05:11.276
Civics is not taught
in school anymore.

00:05:11.276 --> 00:05:14.013
So we were like, "This has to be
something that we start

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:16.949
at a young age, teaching kids
about the process."

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:19.785
And she came up with this
amazing idea and asked me

00:05:19.785 --> 00:05:21.253
to help, you know,
come in with her.

00:05:21.253 --> 00:05:24.357
And Barack and Michelle
came and produced it.

00:05:24.357 --> 00:05:26.659
And I was like, "Yeah.
I mean, I guess."

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:28.627
[ Cheers and applause ]
[ Both laugh ]

00:05:28.627 --> 00:05:30.797
-"Let me think -- yes."
-"I guess. I mean...

00:05:30.797 --> 00:05:32.165
All right."

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:35.634
-So you get Barack Obama
and Michelle Obama, okay.

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:37.603
But are there
any big names involved?

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:38.737
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.737 --> 00:05:40.539
But who else
is involved with this?

00:05:40.539 --> 00:05:42.474
-It's crazy.
It's an animated sort of

00:05:42.474 --> 00:05:46.012
homage of "Schoolhouse Rock."
We got Peter Ramsey,

00:05:46.012 --> 00:05:48.146
who was the animation director
for "Into the Spider-Verse,"

00:05:48.146 --> 00:05:49.648
which was groundbreaking.

00:05:49.648 --> 00:05:51.551
-That was one of the best movies
I've ever seen.

00:05:51.551 --> 00:05:53.952
-It could've won Best Picture.
-I agree.

00:05:53.952 --> 00:05:55.388
I think it should --
Yeah, I loved it.

00:05:55.388 --> 00:05:57.556
-Could've won Best Picture.
So, he's one of the animators.

00:05:57.556 --> 00:06:00.159
We've got an amazing group of,
you know, really diverse

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:02.895
and talented
animation directors.

00:06:02.895 --> 00:06:05.431
Some huge names.
H.E.R. does an amazing song.

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:10.035
Janelle Monae, Adam Lambert,
Brandi Carlile,

00:06:10.035 --> 00:06:13.039
just amazing people
across the board.

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:15.374
And they all come together,
and it's for a good cause,

00:06:15.374 --> 00:06:17.810
and I think from just moving on,

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:21.480
I feel like I want the things
that I do to be about something.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:22.915
You what I'm saying?
Even if it's not something

00:06:22.915 --> 00:06:25.051
that people -- I want people
to start a conversation.

00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:27.786
Even some conversation
that is against me,

00:06:27.786 --> 00:06:29.088
at least it starts
a conversation.

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:31.991
I think this conversation
is about learning what

00:06:31.991 --> 00:06:35.394
this country, at its foundation,
should be about

00:06:35.394 --> 00:06:37.863
and also taking responsibility
for what it's not about.

00:06:37.863 --> 00:06:40.833
And I think that animation
is something that lasts

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:44.636
the test of time, and I'm really
happy to be a part of it.

00:06:44.636 --> 00:06:47.239
-It's called, "We The People,"
4th of July, Netflix.

00:06:47.239 --> 00:06:49.008
Look for it.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:49.008 --> 00:06:52.011
Here's a clip of H.E.R.'s song,
"Change," from "We The People."

00:06:52.011 --> 00:06:53.579
Take a look.

00:06:53.579 --> 00:06:55.681
-♪ Make a statement
and say it proud ♪

00:06:55.681 --> 00:06:59.084
♪ Oh, from the street
to the hill, join a campaign ♪

00:06:59.084 --> 00:07:02.188
♪ Don't have to wait for someday
just to have change ♪

00:07:02.188 --> 00:07:04.724
♪ Nom you're never too young
to make a difference ♪

00:07:04.724 --> 00:07:07.760
♪ You have the power
to be an active citizen ♪

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:13.065
♪ If I'm just one person,
will my voice even stand out ♪

00:07:13.065 --> 00:07:18.237
♪ Can I make a difference
if I don't even know how? ♪

00:07:18.237 --> 00:07:19.671
♪ To change ♪

00:07:19.671 --> 00:07:22.508
♪ I don't even know
how to change ♪

00:07:22.508 --> 00:07:25.477
♪ We don't even know
how to change ♪

00:07:25.477 --> 00:07:30.049
♪ I wanna know how to change ♪

00:07:30.049 --> 00:07:33.285
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:33.285 --> 00:07:35.087
-You have a beautiful mind,
buddy.

00:07:35.087 --> 00:07:36.555
Kenya Barris!

00:07:36.555 --> 00:07:40.226
"We the people" premieres
July 4th, on Netflix!

